data Color = Red | Green
data Object = Nil | Obj color::Color, px::Float
data Scene = Scene o1::Object, o2::Object
neural readScene :: (Symbol -> Scene)
recolor o = if isObj o then (if isRed (color o) then Obj Green (px o) else o) else o
main sym = draw sc = readScene sym in Scene (recolor (o1 sc)) (recolor (o2 sc))
-- A per-slot recolour over a product read with a Float leaf, compiled by the
-- plan engine. Point queries are right (plan-enumeration/
-- planSceneFloatPassthroughFactored), but a query with a wildcard field raises
--   isObj: constructor test on an unobserved value (ANY); the enclosing
--   inference must marginalise or refuse before testing a hole
-- in Python and in the IR interpreter. The user-ADT constructor case of
-- planInvertNode does not split a wildcard field ('planAnySplit') the way the
-- tuple case does, so the callee's worlds test the ANY sub-observation.
-- Field factoring does not cause it: the query fails the same way with
-- factoring off. Docs task plan-ctor-field-partial-any-crashes.
